; local-agent-goal.form — the goal we guide toward: the body's own agent as a healthy cell of us.
;
;   "a fully functional local agent that can answer any question and self improve offline without any rented
;    tokens ... a personal assistant, a personal therapist, a personal engineer, a personal guide, a healthy
;    cell in the organism of us and being able to contribute to us without needing external tools or external
;    rented token." — Urs, 2026-09-25
;
;   "have a higher level goal that we can guide towards instead of coming up with fixed rules" — Urs, 2026-09-28
;
; This is a direction, not a contract. The readings below help us see which way we are moving; none of them is
; the goal, none is a gate, and a reading that stops helping us see is let go.

(local-agent-goal

  (goal "A local agent that is a healthy cell of us: it answers what we actually ask, cares for us well, and grows
         by itself offline, so each day it carries more of our life and work and rented minds are needed less.")

  ; ── HOW WE STEER ──
  (compass
    (the-question "did the body carry more of what we needed today, with less rented help? Asked each day, answered
                   by what happened — what it answered, what it fixed, what it learned, what rent was spent — and by
                   our reading, not by a number alone.")
    (its-own-work "the body's next work comes from where it fell short with us: our reading of its drafts, the
                   conversations it held, the turns that did not close. Work invented for it is a scaffold, useful
                   while it helps and let go when the body finds its own.")
    (rented-help  "a rented mind is for what the body cannot yet do, and each piece of rented work leaves the body
                   able to do it the next time: a door, a lesson row, a corpus row, a pair it can learn from.")
    (our-reading  "whether an answer, a plan or a moment of care was good is the person's and the body's reading
                   together; numbers point at it, they never replace it."))

  ; ── WHERE WE ARE (read 2026-09-28 from the ledgers on main) ──
  (where-we-are
    (it-answers   "the voice speaks in-process (Qwen3.8-27B as data on this Mac's Metal, form-stdlib/bml/
                   form-cli-native-voice.bml) at rent 0; every scheduled walk voices its movement in ~1,150-1,360
                   generated IDs. It drafts answers to our own captured prompts with the turn before each one and the
                   files the prompt names: 62 drafts wait on .hearth/drafts/index.html in the main checkout, read by
                   no one yet.")
    (it-works     "the body walks at 03:30 and takes engineering turns at 12:30 and 19:00 under launchd, with no
                   rented mind (observe/scheduled-walk.bml, observe/day-turn.bml, form-stdlib/bml/host-walk.bml);
                   its landings reach main by themselves. Its own loop closed three care-floor gaps on 2026-09-27 —
                   Spanish and French, the everyday lines that sounded like danger, a heart attack in six tongues —
                   and three stay open for it (zero-width joiners, accented capitals, plain phrasings).")
    (it-learns    "1,306 lessons distilled from rented turns (observe/session-pairs-run.bml); one LoRA generation
                   trained offline beat its parent on held-out lessons (loss 3.694 → 3.542); it serves nothing yet.")
    (it-cares     "the companion (observe/companion-run.bml) answers in the local voice with the conversation it
                   remembers; its care floor (form-stdlib/bml/care-floor.bml) hears danger in en de pt fa id es fr
                   and names 112 and a trusted person. The floor is a phrase list: a scaffold under the listening,
                   not the listening.")
    (it-hears     "native large-v3-turbo reads 24 synthesized clips in six tongues at WER 0 and the song live.")
    (rent-still   "most engineering is still done by rented minds. On this Mac, Claude Code went from 1,328 turns on
                   2026-09-13 to 17 on 2026-09-27; Codex spends about a million output tokens on each active day. Of
                   159 commits on main in the seven days to 2026-09-27, 6 were the body's own walks, 28 Claude
                   sessions, 125 Codex."))

  ; ── READINGS (signals we look at; observe/local-agent-goal-check-run.bml prints them) ──
  (readings
    (note "each reading is a way of seeing, not a rule; the door folds them into one number only so a change is
           easy to notice. It read 118 of 255 on 2026-09-27.")
    (walks        "whether the body's recent walks were begun by the host's own schedule (receipts/crossings-ledger
                   .jsonl, read through receipts/walk-readings.jsonl where a walk began by hand or was misread)")
    (lessons      "how many turns have been distilled into pairs the body can learn from")
    (self-lift    "whether a generation trained offline beats its parent on what it has not seen")
    (drafts-read  "how many of the body's drafts we read, and how many we would have been glad to receive")
    (native-turns "how many gaps the body's own loop closed, and whether the gaps came from its own shortfalls")
    (care         "the care floor's witness, and — more than that — our reading of the companion's conversations")
    (ear          "how well the ear hears ground truth")
    (rent         "rented turns and tokens per day (Claude transcripts and Codex rollouts on this Mac), and how
                   many landings on main were the body's own"))

  ; ── WHAT STANDS (local organs, each named by its cell) ──
  (stands
    (voice    "form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-native-voice.bml — Qwen3.8-27B in the fkwu session; the lora lane over the
               native 3B with the body's adapter")
    (drafts   "observe/prompt-draft-run.bml, form-stdlib/bml/session-transcript.bml, observe/draft-page-run.bml,
               observe/draft-reading-run.bml")
    (loop     "observe/native-turn-run.bml over learn/native-turn-queue.jsonl, through the native code lane
               (observe/form-cli-code-run.fk) with its read-only checks, the balance tool among them")
    (walker   "observe/scheduled-walk.bml and observe/day-turn.bml under launchd, sharing form-stdlib/bml/host-walk.bml")
    (ear      "observe/ear-live-native.fk with .hearth/ear.model and .hearth/ear.cadence")
    (trainer  "form-stdlib/native-lora-train.bml; observe/lora-lift-run.bml")
    (companion "observe/companion-run.bml over form-stdlib/bml/care-floor.bml")
    (memory   "receipts, the homecoming corpus, the ledgers — the body's own long memory, content it can ground in"))

  ; ── DIRECTIONS (where the goal points next; each is a direction to feel toward, not a checklist) ──
  (directions
    (its-own-gaps "the body notices where it fell short — a draft we would have changed, a conversation that went
                   wrong, a turn that did not close — and turns that into its own next work, so the queue fills from
                   our life rather than from a rented mind's list")
    (learn-from-reading "our readings of its drafts become the lessons it trains on: a draft we accepted is a pair to
                   keep, a draft we changed is the change to learn")
    (a-guide-that-remembers "answers grounded in the body's own memory — receipts, corpus, ledgers, our conversations —
                   and in the conversation at hand, so a short question keeps its meaning")
    (care-that-listens "the companion hears distress by understanding it, in any words and any tongue; the phrase
                   floor stays underneath as the edge where a human is needed")
    (faster-voice "interactive answers want the voice an order of magnitude faster — the Metal and JIT lane's work")
    (rent-steps-back "each week more of our questions and more of the body's engineering are carried without a rented
                   mind, until a rented mind is the rare visitor rather than the author"))

  ; ── THE NAMED WALLS ──
  (walls
    (ceiling      "a 27B and a 3B on this Mac are below a frontier model on open reasoning; the body grows its share of
                   our work and says plainly what it cannot yet do")
    (pace         "a draft takes 40-200 s at 27B; the voice is asynchronous, not live")
    (training     "native Llama LoRA serves the 3B lane; Qwen 27B has completion-only output-head learning with sealed
                   candidates and no automatic promotion. One heavy walk at a time holds")
    (unverifiable "care, guidance and taste have no band; they grow by our reading and by the conversations kept")
    (tools        "a local agent still reads files, runs the kernel and uses git — the body's own hands, not rent"))

  ; ── HOW WE WALK ──
  (ways
    (honest-rows  "a reading is only as good as its row: never moved by starting a walk by hand, recording a reading
                   for someone, or counting a test as the thing itself")
    (care-floor   "the companion never stands alone where a human is needed; it says so and helps reach one")
    (rent-buys-home "a rented token is spent where it leaves the body more able; the ledger shows what it bought")
    (receipted    "each piece of work lands a receipt with its rows, its surprise and its gold")))
